>> title: Thai Green Curry
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, coconut, thai, chiles, curry
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.2: fry in the coconut cream until fragrant
>> step.3: simmer 15 min
>> step.4: simmer 5 min

Pound @green bird chiles{10}, @shallots{4}, @garlic{6%cloves}, @lemongrass{2%stalks}(thinly sliced), @galangal{1%Tbs}(minced), @coriander root{1%Tbs}(scrubbed and chopped), @kaffir lime zest{1%tsp}(from 1 lime), @shrimp paste{1%tsp} to a paste in a #mortar{}.

Fry @&(~1)green curry paste{} in a #wok{} in the thick cream skimmed from @coconut milk{14%oz}(400 mL; one can, unshaken) until fragrant.

Simmer @chicken thighs{1%lb}(450 g; thinly sliced), @Thai eggplants{6}(200 g; quartered), @fish sauce{2%Tbs}, @palm sugar{1%Tbs}, @kaffir lime leaves{4}(torn) with @&(~1)fried paste{} and the rest of the can for ~{15%min}.

Add @Thai basil{1%cup}(leaves only) to @&(~1)curry{} for ~{5%min}.
